{
  "id": "reverse-linked-list-ii",
  "questionId": "reverse-linked-list-ii",
  "slug": "reverse-linked-list-ii",
  "title": "Reverse Linked List II",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Linked list",
  "patterns": [
    "linked list",
    "in-place reversal"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "you only need to touch the nodes from left to right - can you avoid rebuilding the parts before and after?",
    "walk to just before position left and remember that node - everything before it never moves",
    "within the sublist, repeatedly take the node right after your reversal point and move it to the very front of the sublist (a technique sometimes called 'head insertion')",
    "do this (right - left) times, then reconnect: the node before position left should now point to what was originally the node at position right"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "losing track of the node just before position left, which is needed to reconnect the reversed sublist",
    "off-by-one errors converting 1-indexed left/right into how many swaps or moves are needed",
    "forgetting to reconnect the tail of the reversed sublist to whatever originally followed position right"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A singly linked list is given to you as an array `nums`, where `nums[i]`\nis the value of the i-th node in order, along with two positions `left`\nand `right`.\n\n**Reverse only the sublist that runs from position `left` to position `right`, inclusive (1-indexed), leaving the rest of the list untouched, and return the resulting full list's values in order.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= nums.length <= 500",
      "-500 <= nums[i] <= 500",
      "1 <= left <= right <= nums.length"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "left equals right (single node, no visible change)",
      "left = 1 (reversal starts at the head)",
      "right = nums.length (reversal ends at the tail)",
      "left = 1 and right = nums.length (reverse the whole list)"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], left = 2, right = 4",
        "output": "[1, 4, 3, 2, 5]",
        "expectedOutput": "[1, 4, 3, 2, 5]",
        "explanation": "positions 2 through 4 (values 2, 3, 4) are reversed to 4, 3, 2; positions 1 and 5 stay put"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [5], left = 1, right = 1",
        "output": "[5]",
        "expectedOutput": "[5]",
        "explanation": "reversing a single node changes nothing"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], left = 1, right = 5",
        "output": "[5, 4, 3, 2, 1]",
        "expectedOutput": "[5, 4, 3, 2, 1]",
        "explanation": "reversing the entire list is the same as full reversal"
      }
    ],
